{"units": [{"id": "presbys-quote4", "translation": "Hail, old man"}, {"id": "presbys-quote5", "translation": "And you, elders, hail"}, {"id": "presbys-word1", "translation": "Appellation honorific for men of princely rank"}, {"id": "presbytes-orth1", "translation": "old man"}, {"id": "presbytes-def1", "translation": "old man"}, {"id": "presbytes-quote1", "translation": "He bound his father, old Cronus"}, {"id": "presbytis-orth1", "translation": "old woman, advanced in age"}, {"id": "presbytis-def1", "translation": "old woman, advanced in age"}, {"id": "presbytis-quote1", "translation": "A young man rides me down, an old woman"}, {"id": "presbytis-quote2", "translation": "a band of old women"}, {"id": "presbytodokos-orth1", "translation": "receiving old men"}, {"id": "presbytodokos-def1", "translation": "receiving old men"}, {"id": "presbytodokos-note1", "translation": "Hermann adds προβούλοις [to the councilors]"}, {"id": "presbytodokos-quote1", "translation": "Let the altars that receive old men blaze for the venerable ones"}, {"id": "presbytodokos-word1", "translation": "to the councilors"}, {"id": "preumenes-orth1", "translation": "kindly, gentle, gracious"}, {"id": "preumenes-def1", "translation": "kindly, gentle, gracious"}, {"id": "preumenes-note1", "translation": "πρευμενεῖς [kindly ones] in the copies"}, {"id": "preumenes-quote1", "translation": "bringing kindly libations from a son to his father"}, {"id": "preumenes-quote2", "translation": "and I received the libations kindly"}, {"id": "preumenes-quote3", "translation": "seeming to be very kindly disposed to me"}, {"id": "preumenes-quote4", "translation": "having come here with kindly fortune"}, {"id": "preumenes-quote5", "translation": "and in time may the all-seeing father bring kindly endings"}, {"id": "preumenes-quote6", "translation": "may he look with a kindly eye"}, {"id": "preumenes-quote7", "translation": "kindly to the bridegrooms"}, {"id": "preumenes-word1", "translation": "kindly ones"}, {"id": "preumenos-orth1", "translation": "kindly"}, {"id": "preumenos-def1", "translation": "kindly"}, {"id": "preumenos-quote1", "translation": "and kindly from him, your husband Darius, to send good things to you"}, {"id": "preumenos-quote2", "translation": "being a prophet of these things, I kindly advised you"}, {"id": "preumenos-quote3", "translation": "and kindly bring in this stranger woman"}, {"id": "preumenos-quote4", "translation": "and receive kindly the avenger"}, {"id": "preumenos-quote5", "translation": "which I, having prophesied, kindly pray for"}, {"id": "priamides-orth1", "translation": "sons of Priam"}, {"id": "priamides-def1", "translation": "sons of Priam"}, {"id": "priamides-note1", "translation": "where the first syllable is lengthened in Ionic meter, as in the dactylic verses of both Greek and Latin poets."}, {"id": "priamides-quote1", "translation": "and the sons of Priam paid double penalties"}, {"id": "priamides-quote2", "translation": "rushing upon the sons of Priam"}, {"id": "priamides-quote3", "translation": "justice came to the sons of Priam in time"}, {"id": "priamos-orth1", "translation": "Priam, king of Troy"}, {"id": "priamos-def1", "translation": "Priam, king of Troy"}, {"id": "priamos-note1", "translation": "whence Πριάμου πόλις [the city of Priam] is Troy."}, {"id": "priamos-quote1", "translation": "the great adversary of Priam"}, {"id": "priamos-quote2", "translation": "the city of Priam"}, {"id": "priamos-quote3", "translation": "for the Argives have taken the city of Priam"}, {"id": "priamos-quote4", "translation": "the ancient city of Priam"}, {"id": "priamos-quote5", "translation": "the city of Priam"}, {"id": "priamos-quote6", "translation": "What do you think Priam would have done if he had accomplished these things?"}, {"id": "priamos-word1", "translation": "the city of Priam, T"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-orth1", "translation": "before, formerly, once"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-def1", "translation": "before, formerly, once"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-def2", "translation": "With the article"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-def3", "translation": "τὸ πρίν [formerly]"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-note1", "translation": "by rule it is short in all poets from Homer onward, except that epic poets often lengthened it in the dactylic arsis, on which see Thes. vol. 6 p. 1598"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-quote1", "translation": "Yet with such self-willed acts even before you brought yourself into these troubles"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-quote2", "translation": "nor will it be said before"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-quote3", "translation": "I said it also before"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-quote4", "translation": "and the former monstrous things he now destroys"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-quote5", "translation": "you accomplished your former need from me lightly"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-quote6", "translation": "for we endured many former evils"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-quote7", "translation": "of the former entrances"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-quote8", "translation": "the former prosperity"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-quote9", "translation": "being foolish formerly"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-quote10", "translation": "but someone formerly believing in gods nowhere"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-quote11", "translation": "being most hostile formerly"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-quote12", "translation": "and reverence unconquerable, untamed, unwarlike formerly"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-quote13", "translation": "a truthful prophet formerly"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-quote14", "translation": "a kindred marriage formerly"}, {"id": "prin-adverb-word1", "translation": "formerly"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-orth1", "translation": "before, until"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-def1", "translation": "before, until"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-def2", "translation": "With the aorist infinitive"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-def3", "translation": "Twice with the present infinitive"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-def4", "translation": "πρὶν ἂν [before] with the subjunctive after a negative sentence, on which construction see Thes. vol. 6 p. 1600. 1601 and in the Lexicon Sophocleum."}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-note1", "translation": "conjunction"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-note2", "translation": "πρίν γ᾽ ἐγώ σφισιν ἔδειξα κράσεις [before I showed them the mixtures]"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-note3", "translation": "γ᾽ [indeed] is omitted in several copies. With the aorist indicative"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-note4", "translation": "thus Porson for χράναι [to anoint]"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-quote1", "translation": "which he had toiled through before coming here"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-quote2", "translation": "before the blasts of Ares rush down"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-quote3", "translation": "before the swift messengers arrive"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-quote4", "translation": "before entering my house"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-quote5", "translation": "before casting this land into danger"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-quote6", "translation": "before the rays of the god are scattered"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-quote7", "translation": "before seeing the depth of evils"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-quote8", "translation": "before the ancient grief ceases"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-quote9", "translation": "before seeing this man"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-quote10", "translation": "before suffering"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-quote11", "translation": "before he speaks"}, {"id": "prin-coniunctio-quote12", "translation": "before setting foot on this muddy land"}]}